<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rouen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rotomagus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rouen is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, historic capital of Normandy. As Rotomagus it was the chief town of the Gallic Veliocasses and a Roman river port. Granted with the surrounding land to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a> in 911, it became the capital of the Duchy of Normandy and one of the largest towns of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> was tried and burned there in 1431, and its Gothic cathedral was painted many times by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claude-monet">Monet</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rouen.jpg" alt="Rouen" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Herbert Frank from Wien (Vienna), AT · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rouen_(37903223574).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Scandinavian raiders had attacked the river valley since the 840s, and by the early tenth century a band led by Rollo had established itself around <b>Rouen</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Duchy of Normandy · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>He recovered much of the southern Netherlands for Spain, took Antwerp after a celebrated siege in 1584–1585, and led the Army of Flanders into France to relieve Paris in 1590 and <b>Rouen</b> in 1592; he became duke in 1586 but never returned to rule in person.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 911 Charles the Simple granted the leader Rollo lands around <b>Rouen</b>, the origin of the Duchy of Normandy.</blockquote><a href="/culture/vikings">Vikings · Contact &amp; Exchange</a></li><li><blockquote>After a six-month siege that left thousands starving, <b>Rouen</b> yielded to Henry V of England, completing his conquest of Normandy.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-19">19 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The failure led to the Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte, by which King Charles the Simple granted Rollo lands around <b>Rouen</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-20">20 July in history</a></li><li><blockquote>They sold her to the English, who had her tried for heresy and burned at <b>Rouen</b> a year later.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-23">23 May in history</a></li></ul></section>
